    "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",
    "note": "Wave-1 row 17 named the Panda from Quaternius's Animated Animals on poly.pizza, which sits behind a Cloudflare challenge (and Quaternius's Google Drive is quota-blocked), so it is unreachable. Two reachable CC0 pandas were rendered: the Panda from Quaternius's Textured Cute Monster Pack (Aug 2020, OpenGameArt) and this one from Kenney Cube Pets. The monster-pack panda is a head-shaped blob with no legs, and its painted grey texture clusters into 17 near-identical greys that scatter the eye patches over the face, so it does not read as a panda in the cel look. The Cube Pets panda has clean black eye patches, ears, shoulder band and legs on white, and reads as a panda at a glance; it is deliberately blocky. Colour map flattened to 24 clusters: the 14 slate clusters (#3d-#52) -> patch, the 10 white clusters -> fur. Ground: run is a hop (in the air up to 5 cm between strides, as authored) and clamps so the landings never sink; walk is a bouncy trot that never sinks and is left as authored; eat lets the snout dip (sinkAllowed). Ingested through Blender like the other Cube Pets (the gltf route cannot load the external colormap.png in Node and would not flatten it)."
  },
